body:
@hijirii As noted on your previous closed PR (#2989), this is a duplicate of my actively maintained PR (#2984) which fixes #2322. 

While AI agents and automated tools can be a great asset to open-source when they abide by community norms, the automation being used here is ignoring repository context. A well-configured agent should recognize when an open PR already exists for an issue, rather than scraping feedback from contributors to blindly duplicate the effort. Re-opening a duplicated PR like this just creates unnecessary noise and review burden.

**Note to maintainers:** PR #2984 contains the original implementation of this fix.
